[38;5;231m⏺[39m I opened a browser tab with mockups, since layout is easier to judge by seeing it:
  [94m]8;id=17ifz8n;http://localhost:53837/?key=6e2194c2226a7413cdc5ecdecf16b3e1f773b7064f5c32694eab8356d902c142\http://localhost:53837/?key=6e2194c2226a7413cdc5ecdecf16b3e1f773b7064f5c32694eab8356d902c142[39m]8;;\ (the mockups use a lot of
  tokens; tell me if you'd rather stay in the terminal).

  All three options use the same four groups, taken from the 12 fields in [38;5;153mpublic/settings.html[39m:

  - [1mProfile:[0m display name, email, avatar URL
  - [1mPreferences:[0m time zone, language, theme
  - [1mNotifications:[0m email, push, weekly digest
  - [1mSecurity:[0m two-factor auth, session timeout, API token

  The tab compares three ways to lay them out:

  - [1mA. Stacked sections[0m (my recommendation): headed fieldsets on one page. You can still scan everything, and only the
    HTML and CSS change.
  - [1mB. Bordered cards:[0m the same structure as A, but each group sits in a box so the separation is stronger.
  - [1mC. Sidebar tabs:[0m one group visible at a time. This needs new JS and is more machinery than 12 fields call for.

  In every option the field [38;5;153mname[39ms and the single Save button stay the same, so [38;5;153msettings.js[39m and the data posted to
  [38;5;153m/api/settings[39m don't change.

  Which layout do you want? Click one in the browser or answer here. If the groupings look wrong, say that too.

  The mockup files are in [38;5;153m.hyperpowers/[39m inside the repo. There's no [38;5;153m.gitignore[39m yet, so you may want to add that folder
  to one.

